== Synergies ==
* {{t|Baby-Bender}}: Wisps gain homing tears.
* {{i|BFFS!}}: Increases the tear size and doubles the damage of wisps.
* {{Book of Belial synergy|description=Can be stacked along with The Book of Belial, allowing you to carry 2 passive books and an activated item on top of them.}}
* {{t|'M}}: If an active item is combined with the Book, only the active item is rerolled; the Book remains unchanged. If no active item is combined with the Book, the Book will be rerolled on use. 'M also cannot give Book of Virtues from rerolling other items, as it is considered a passive item.
* {{i|Car Battery}}: Doubles the spawned wisps on activation.
* {{i|Glowing Hourglass}}: Its wisps are kept between uses, allowing for wisp farming on the current floor by picking up Glowing Hourglass and using it to go back to the previous room before Glowing Hourglass was picked up.
* {{i|Tear Detonator}}: The wisps' tears are also detonated; the resulting tears are based on Isaac's own, rather than the wisps'.

== Interactions ==
* {{i|Analog Stick}}: Wisps are unable to shoot diagonally, and will shoot orthogonally instead.
* {{i|Lodestone}}: The wisps' tears are attracted to the magnetic enemy, making it much easier to connect all of the wisps' tears on an enemy.
* {{t|NO!}}: Will not prevent Book of Virtues from spawning, as it's considered a passive item.
* {{i|Void}}: Book of Virtues is considered to be a passive item, so stat boosts will be gained by using Void on it and further uses of Void will not have the Book's effects.
* {{p|XVII - The Stars?}}: Book of Virtues will be removed if it's the oldest collected item, even if another active item is not being held.

